      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Timorous Falls [zone=1325]\n**Who:**\n- Koff Plasterfoot [ _Quests_]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 120\n**Maximum Level:** | 130\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n**Related Creatures:**\n- a cliff hawk [npc=59332]\n- a parched corvid [npc=59347]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Mercenary of Timorous Falls (15 Points) [quest=12652]\n**Era:** | !Laurion's Song\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Fri Nov 3 03:21:02 2023\nModified: Sun Jan 21 19:55:37 2024 | | **Laurion's Song Info & Guides: Overview \\| Progression & Task List \\| Raiding \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\nYou can obtain this solo task from Koff Plasterfoot [npc=59380] in Timorous Falls. You can find Gunder at /waypoint -2340, -1584, -81 in the south part of the zone in front of the bridge to the fortress. He is on the find tool as well CTRL F.\nYou say, 'Hail, Koff Plasterfoot'\nKoff Plasterfoot says, 'Welcome to Eureka's Tumble, fellow roamer! Your outfit tells me that you are not from around these parts. It's okay though. Maddie is a great host and does a fine job making sure everyone is welcome under her roof, so long as they don't start any [trouble] with people who are just trying to enjoy their drinks. I'm Koff Plasterfoot, and I'm a worker at Eureka's Tumble, as you might have guessed. You may be wondering, 'Why do they keep calling it Maddie's Steppe?' Well, my friend, it's because Maddie named it and it's her steppe. Do please try to keep up.'\nYou say, 'Trouble you say? Everyone seems so jolly.'\nKoff Plasterfoot says, 'Indeed! You may have noticed that to the southeast of the tavern is a local constabulary. Pay no heed to them. They are mainly here to keep the caravans safe. The ale that Maddie creates is something special and orders for shipments all over the world can be found here. That cargo is precious, and needs protecting. Which is actually why I am elated to meet you out here! You look like someone who has had their fair share of [menial tasks] given to them. What's another for the books?'\nYou say, 'I've had to do so many menial tasks already. How can I help?'\nKoff Plasterfoot says, 'See! You get it! Us roamers don't sit in one space for too long. I understand! You gotta get your coin for a drink! Which is why I am happy to speak with you. You see, the critters to the north of here have been getting spooked out of the forest and have been seen wandering too close to the trails. This has caused panic amongst the shipping lines, as these critters are not too picky about who they attack after being driven from their homes. We have a few menaces that could use some population management. We could use some help getting rid of some [mosquitos], as well as quieting the [raptors], and finally those [vines] near the wheat fields. If you're feeling extra frisky, you can help us with [all three].'\nYou say, 'Those raptors won't know what hit them!'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Bird Boxing'.\nKoff Plasterfoot says, 'They peck at the caravans from above. You'd think that taking a few out would cause them to back off from the caravans, but it only agitates them more. Getting rid of them will be a blessing for us. Ravens and magpies have also been a problem and we will be better off with less of them pecking at us as well.'\n\n---\n\nThe various avians in Timorous Falls have been known to attack caravans that enter the area, due to being pushed out of their forest home to the north. Clear out as many of them as you can find so the caravans can continue without further incident.\n1\\. Fight the Falcons 0/8 Timorous Falls\nYou can find these birds on the southwest side of the zone near the cliff. This includes a cliff hawk [npc=59332] and a parched corvid.\n\n---\n\nNote: Clicking on 'all three' in the quest text assigns all 3 of Koff's tasks at once, additional text:\nYou say, 'Let's nip all three of them in the bud!'\nKoff Plasterfoot says, 'Hot diggity dang! We got a live one here! Thanks! The Falls will be better after you are done.'\n\n---\n\nReward(s):\n141 platinum 6 gold 6 silver 7 copper\nYou gain experience!\n**Submitted by:** Gidono",
